				&lt;tr style="height:14.35pt"&gt;&#xD;
					&lt;td style="width:139.55pt; padding:0.25pt 5.65pt; vertical-align:bottom"&gt;&#xD;
						&lt;p style="margin-top:0pt; margin-bottom:0pt; font-size:9pt"&gt;&#xD;
							&lt;span style="font-family:'Times New Roman'"&gt;Total other noncurrent assets&lt;/span&gt;&#xD;
						&lt;/p&gt;&#xD;
					&lt;/td&gt;&#xD;
					&lt;td style="width:86pt; border-top-style:solid; border-top-width:0.75pt; border-bottom-style:double; border-bottom-width:2.25pt; padding-top:0.03pt; padding-right:5.65pt; padding-left:5.65pt; vertical-align:bottom"&gt;&#xD;
						&lt;p style="margin-top:0pt; margin-bottom:0pt; font-size:9pt"&gt;&#xD;
							&lt;span style="font-family:'Times New Roman'"&gt;$&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="width:31.5pt; display:inline-block"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:'Times New Roman'"&gt; 18,445,066&lt;/span&gt;&#xD;
						&lt;/p&gt;&#xD;
					&lt;/td&gt;&#xD;
					&lt;td style="width:0.65pt; padding:0.25pt 5.65pt; vertical-align:bottom"&gt;&#xD;
						&lt;p style="margin-top:0pt; margin-bottom:0pt; font-size:9pt"&gt;&#xD;
							&lt;span style="font-family:'Times New Roman'"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&#xD;
						&lt;/p&gt;&#xD;
					&lt;/td&gt;&#xD;
					&lt;td style="width:1.85pt; padding:0.25pt 5.65pt; vertical-align:bottom"&gt;&#xD;
						&lt;p style="margin-top:0pt; margin-bottom:0pt; font-size:9pt"&gt;&#xD;
							&lt;span style="font-family:'Times New Roman'"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&#xD;
						&lt;/p&gt;&#xD;
					&lt;/td&gt;&#xD;
					&lt;td style="width:81.1pt; border-top-style:solid; border-top-width:0.75pt; border-bottom-style:double; border-bottom-width:2.25pt; padding-top:0.03pt; padding-right:5.65pt; padding-left:5.65pt; vertical-align:bottom"&gt;&#xD;
						&lt;p style="margin-top:0pt; margin-bottom:0pt; font-size:9pt"&gt;&#xD;
							&lt;span style="font-family:'Times New Roman'"&gt;$&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="width:31.5pt; display:inline-block"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:'Times New Roman'"&gt;14,179,835&lt;/span&gt;&#xD;
						&lt;/p&gt;&#xD;
					&lt;/td&gt;&#xD;
					&lt;td style="width:0.65pt; padding:0.25pt 5.65pt; vertical-align:bottom"&gt;&#xD;
						&lt;p style="margin-top:0pt; margin-bottom:0pt; font-size:9pt"&gt;&#xD;
							&lt;span style="font-family:'Times New Roman'"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&#xD;
						&lt;/p&gt;&#xD;
					&lt;/td&gt;&#xD;
				&lt;/tr&gt;&#xD;
			&lt;/table&gt;&#xD;
			&lt;p style="margin-top:0pt; margin-bottom:0pt; font-size:12pt"&gt;&#xD;
				&lt;span style="font-family:'Times New Roman'"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&#xD;
			&lt;/p&gt;&#xD;
			&lt;p style="margin-top:0pt; margin-bottom:8pt; line-height:108%; font-size:10pt"&gt;&#xD;
				&lt;span style="font-family:Arial"&gt;The Company maintains certain volumes of product&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:Arial"&gt; in its pipeline systems and storage tanks to ensure efficient operation of the pipeline system. These volumes, referred to as line fill and tank heel, are necessary to maintain the integrity and functionality of the pipeline system. During 2024, the method of accounting for operational volumes for tank heel was expanded to include line fill volume.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:Arial"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:Arial"&gt;The tank heel represents minimum volume of product required for the operation of the tank and are recorded at historical cost.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:Arial"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:Arial"&gt;The line fill represents product &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:Arial"&gt;volume required for the operation of the pipeline within &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:Arial"&gt;facilities and are recorded at historical cost. These volumes are not available for sale and are considered part of the Company&amp;#x2019;s operational requirements. The cost associated with line fill and tank heel is capitalized and included in Other Noncurrent Assets on the balance sheet. The Company periodically reviews the volumes of line fill and tank heel to ensure they meet operational needs and adjusts them based on changes in the pipeline and storage i&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:Arial"&gt;nfrastructure. &lt;/span&gt;&#xD;
			&lt;/p&gt;&#xD;
			&lt;p style="margin-top:0pt; margin-bottom:8pt; line-height:108%; font-size:10pt"&gt;&#xD;
				&lt;span style="font-family:Arial"&gt;The Company holds a 33% ownership interest in Transport 4 (&amp;#x201C;T4&amp;#x201D;), a privately held limited liability c&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:Arial"&gt;ompany. The Company held a 25% ownership interest until June 2025 at which time the Company purchased an additional 8% interest, bringing the total holding to 33%. The investment is accounted for under the equity method of accounting because the Company has the ability to exercise significant influence over T4&amp;#x2019;s operating and financial policies. The carrying value of the investment in T4 as December 31, 2025 and 2024, was $5,467,007 and $1,937,646, respectively, and is included in Other Noncurrent Assets in&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:Arial"&gt; the accompanying consolidated balance sheet.&lt;/span&gt;&#xD;
			&lt;/p&gt;&#xD;
			&lt;p style="margin-top:12pt; margin-bottom:0pt; line-height:12pt; widows:0; orphans:0"&gt;&#xD;
				&lt;span style="font-family:Arial; font-size:10pt"&gt;The Company&amp;#x2019;s share of T4&amp;#x2019;s net income for the years ended December 31, 2025, and 2024 was $2,238,496 and $1,546,052, respectively, and is included in Other Income in the accompanying consolidated statements of income and retained earnings. The Company received cash distributions for the years ended December 31, 2025, and 2024 were $1,292,468 and $1,125,000, respectively. These distributions were recorded as a reduction of the investment&amp;#x2019;s carrying amount.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:'Swis721 BT'; font-size:9pt"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:Arial; font-size:10pt"&gt;The Company uses the cumulative earnings approach to classify distributions from its equity method investment and considers distributions received which do not exceed cumulative equity in earnings subsequent to the date of investment to be a return on investment and are classified as operating activities in the consolidated statements of cash flows. The carrying value of the Company's investment at December 31, 2025 approximates the Company's underlying equity in the net assets of T4.&lt;/span&gt;&#xD;
			&lt;/p&gt;&#xD;
			&lt;p style="margin-top:0pt; margin-bottom:8pt; line-height:108%; font-size:10pt"&gt;&#xD;
				&lt;span style="font-family:Arial"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&#xD;
			&lt;/p&gt;&#xD;
			&lt;p style="margin-top:0pt; margin-bottom:0pt; font-size:12pt"&gt;&#xD;
				&lt;span style="font-family:'Times New Roman'"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&#xD;
			&lt;/p&gt;&#xD;
			&lt;p style="margin-top:0pt; margin-bottom:0pt; font-size:12pt"&gt;&#xD;
				&lt;span style="font-family:'Times New Roman'"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&#xD;
			&lt;/p&gt;&#xD;
			&lt;ol start="10" type="a" style="margin:0pt; padding-left:0pt"&gt;&#xD;
				&lt;li style="margin-left:18pt; margin-bottom:10pt; text-indent:-18pt; page-break-after:avoid; font-family:Arial; font-size:10pt; font-weight:bold; font-style:italic; list-style-position:inside; -aw-list-padding-sml:16.49pt"&gt;&#xD;
					&lt;span style="font:7pt 'Times New Roman'; "&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:'Times New Roman'; font-size:7pt; font-weight:normal; font-style:normal"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:'Times New Roman'; font-size:7pt; font-weight:normal; font-style:normal"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:'Times New Roman'; font-size:7pt; font-weight:normal; font-style:normal"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:'Times New Roman'; font-size:7pt; font-weight:normal; font-style:normal"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:'Times New Roman'; font-size:7pt; font-weight:normal; font-style:normal"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:'Times New Roman'; font-size:7pt; font-weight:normal; font-style:normal"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:'Times New Roman'; font-size:7pt; font-weight:normal; font-style:normal"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:'Times New Roman'; font-size:7pt; font-weight:normal; font-style:normal"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:'Times New Roman'; font-size:7pt; font-weight:normal; font-style:normal"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:'Times New Roman'; font-size:7pt; font-weight:normal; font-style:normal"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:'Times New Roman'; font-size:7pt; font-weight:normal; font-style:normal"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:'Times New Roman'; font-size:7pt; font-weight:normal; font-style:normal"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;Other Current Liabilities&lt;/span&gt;&#xD;
				&lt;/li&gt;&#xD;
			&lt;/ol&gt;&#xD;
